PowerPC registers in the machine context.

2.52 knows the PowerPC stack pointer and nothing else about the processor.
The frame pointer is r31, the faulting address srr0, arguments from r3.
And the thread state is reached as ss rather than __ss before 10.5.

Wasm and the LLInt program counter name a register only so that the file
compiles: neither is in use on a processor that runs the C interpreter.

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/MachineContext.h	2026-09-23 00:42:00
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/MachineContext.h	2026-09-23 00:43:55
@@ -36,6 +36,19 @@
 
 WTF_ALLOW_UNSAFE_BUFFER_USAGE_BEGIN
 
+// PowerPC Mac OS X. The thread state is reached as ss rather than __ss
+// before the UNIX 03 conformance of 10.5, and its registers have the plain
+// names. The registers are the PowerPC ABI's: r1 is the stack pointer, r31
+// the frame pointer, srr0 the address a fault happened at, r3 onwards the
+// arguments.
+#if CP_OLD_DARWIN
+#define CP_THREAD_STATE(context) ((context)->ss)
+#define CP_PPC(regs, name) ((regs).name)
+#else
+#define CP_THREAD_STATE(context) ((context)->__ss)
+#define CP_PPC(regs, name) ((regs).__##name)
+#endif
+
 namespace JSC {
 namespace MachineContext {
 
